# Nothing to configure.
#
# This file used to offer a `GEMINI_API_KEY` slot. There has been nothing to
# give a Gemini key *to* since 24 July, when `server.ts` was deleted along with
# the `POST /api/gemini/assistant` route it served — an open, unmetered,
# unauthenticated proxy that spent the owner's quota for anyone who could reach
# the port. See ../README.md.
#
# A key placeholder for a deleted endpoint is worse than no file at all: it
# reads as a setup step, so the first person to clone this repository pastes a
# real credential into a mock that will never send it anywhere. The AI panel now
# says plainly that the archive has no backend, and asks for nothing.
#
# `react-app/` still builds and runs as a static mock:
#
#   npm install && npm run dev
